- Decision: NotABug
- Reason: The target bug was the partially initialized `struct tc_skbmod opt` passed to `nla_put(..., sizeof(opt), &opt)`. Its padding could be copied to userspace; the fix zeroes the whole structure before assigning fields. The reported source already contains that fix, so the target leak is no longer present.

  The warning instead points to `nla_put_64bit()` copying `struct tcf_t t`, after `tcf_tm_dump()` fills it. `struct tcf_t` contains three `u64` fields and has no padding hole to leak. Thus this report does not identify the target bug in the shown code.

